“…Christ who strengthens me.” — Philippians 4:13.

And there’s a deeper layer to that verse.

Paul was talking about learning to endure both abundance and hardship, not simply being able to accomplish anything imaginable.

Strength isn’t only the power to conquer. It’s also the power to endure, remain faithful, find contentment, and keep going.

And through the lens we’ve been exploring: the same reality can be experienced differently depending on what gives a person strength, meaning, and purpose.

Faith doesn’t have to eliminate uncertainty to help someone face it.

All things through faith. All things through love. All things through the life we choose to live.

Different expressions, different layers—and sometimes overlapping stories. 🤜🏻